    {
      "title": "Netanyahu bloc loses majority as most ballots counted – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/israel-election-results-live-updates-exit-polls-netanyahu-likud-eisenkot-latest-news",
      "description": "<p>This live blog is now closed – you can read the latest elections news <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/israel-election-exit-polls-suggest-netanyahu-eisenkot-blocs-tied-ntwnfb\">here</a></p><p><strong>One apparent loser from Tuesday’s election was far-right national security minister Itamar Ben-Gvir, who was expected to better his party’s result of six seats from the 2022 elections.</strong></p><p>But instead there was stunned silence at the watch party for Otzma Yehudit (Jewish Power) in central Israel as results from the exit polls flashed across the screen, with most channels suggesting the party would remain on just six seats.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/israel-election-results-live-updates-exit-polls-netanyahu-likud-eisenkot-latest-news\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-29T00:24:12"
    },
    {
      "title": "Coalition talks loom in Israel as Netanyahu and Eisenkot blocs set to fall short of majority",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/israel-election-exit-polls-suggest-netanyahu-eisenkot-blocs-tied-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Projections show votes for Palestinian parties surged in a tight contest that drew highest turnout in decades</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/israel-election-results-what-we-know-so-far-ntwnfb\">Israel election: what we know so far</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/27/palestinian-parties-knesset-election-exit-polls-redraw-israel-political-landscape\">Analysis: Rise of Palestinian parties in Knesset will redraw Israel’s political landscape</a></p></li></ul><p>Israel’s future hung in the balance on Wednesday as it became clear that Benjamin Netanyahu had lost his governing majority. His political fate now depends on whether opposition Jewish parties are prepared to forge a common front with Palestinian parties, whose support surged in Tuesday’s elections.</p><p>The leader of the Jewish opposition bloc, the retired general Gadi Eisenkot, appeared to rule out such a broad coalition in a premature declaration of victory overnight for what he called a “Zionist majority”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/israel-election-exit-polls-suggest-netanyahu-eisenkot-blocs-tied-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-28T19:58:27"
    },
    {
      "title": "Israel’s choice: Netanyahu remaining in power or a Palestinian-backed coalition",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/israel-elections-choice-netanyahu-remaining-power-or-palestinian-backed-coalition",
      "description": "<p>Incumbent could turn defeat into another term in office as rival parties erect confected barrier to unseating him</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/israel-election-exit-polls-suggest-netanyahu-eisenkot-blocs-tied-ntwnfb\">Full report: Coalition talks loom in Israel</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/27/palestinian-parties-knesset-election-exit-polls-redraw-israel-political-landscape\">Analysis: Rise of Palestinian parties will redraw political landscape</a></p></li></ul><p>Hours before the final results from <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/28/israel-election-results-live-updates-exit-polls-netanyahu-likud-eisenkot-latest-news\">Israel’s elections</a> were in, several things were clear. Benjamin Netanyahu’s far-right coalition had lost its mandate, and the opposition had a firm majority.</p><p>But most of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel\">Israel</a>’s Jewish opposition ruled out governing with Palestinian-led parties, in the course of a racist election campaign in which Netanyahu painted Palestinian citizens as an enemy inside the state.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/israel-elections-choice-netanyahu-remaining-power-or-palestinian-backed-coalition\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-28T18:54:10"
    },
